Description: Unofficial R port of 'CroCoDeEL' version 1.3.1
    <https://github.com/metagenopolis/CroCoDeEL>, a tool that detects
    cross-sample (well-to-well) contamination in shotgun metagenomic data
    from species abundance tables alone. For each sample pair, a
    contamination line is searched in the scatterplot of log abundances
    and a Random Forest model scores the pair. The default model of the
    original tool is included without retraining. Models can be trained
    with 'ranger'. Not affiliated with or endorsed by the authors of
    'CroCoDeEL'.
